-- How many bill checks the owner has spent.
--
-- Its own table because it is its own balance. Checks and scans shared `scan_usage`, so five
-- scanned bills closed the check — the owner had spent nothing on it, and the wall arrived
-- because they had used the app the way it asks to be used.
--
-- **Deliberately not syncable**, for the same reason as `scan_usage`: the cap is a commercial
-- limit on something that costs nothing to run, not a cost control, and counting it
-- server-side would need an account the app does not require. A reinstall clears it, which is
-- accepted (docs/PAYWALL_PLAN.md, decision 4).
--
-- One row, pinned. The cap is a lifetime one, so there is no period to key on — unlike
-- `scan_usage`, whose per-month rows are a leftover from when its cap reset.
CREATE TABLE bill_check_usage (
    id          INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    check_count INTEGER NOT NULL
);

countAll:
SELECT check_count
FROM bill_check_usage
WHERE id = 1;

-- Insert-then-update in one transaction, not an UPSERT: `ON CONFLICT ... DO UPDATE` needs
-- SQLite 3.24 and minSdk 26 ships 3.18. The insert is ignored once the row exists, so on
-- every later check the update is what counts.
start:
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO bill_check_usage (id, check_count)
VALUES (1, 0);

increment:
UPDATE bill_check_usage
SET check_count = check_count + 1
WHERE id = 1;
